  "body": "Currently we say variables are block scoped, implying the following is OK:\r\n\r\n1. Let _x_ be \"foo\"\r\n1. If _y_ is \"bar\", then\r\n   1. Let _x_ be 5\r\n   2. Print _x_\r\n1. Print _x_\r\n\r\nand that it will print 5, then \"foo\".\r\n\r\nShould we just say that you're not supposed to declare the same variable multiple times per algorithm, i.e. you cannot \"shadow\" variable names? Or we could discourage it, without prohibiting it?",
